WEBVTT

00:56.556 --> 01:00.977
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:01.061 --> 01:03.897
WANT SOME PORK BELLY?

01:10.028 --> 01:11.946
What am I doing here?

01:12.030 --> 01:14.157
What do you think? You're cleaning grills.

01:14.949 --> 01:16.618
Make sure to clean them thoroughly.

01:16.701 --> 01:18.286
Look, these aren't clean at all.

01:18.369 --> 01:20.121
I can't believe I trusted this nutcase

01:20.205 --> 01:22.373
when she said
she'd take me someplace nice.

01:22.457 --> 01:23.374
This is someplace nice.

01:23.458 --> 01:26.294
You can work out and also smell the meat.

01:29.172 --> 01:30.757
Grilled pork jowls, pork neck,

01:31.341 --> 01:32.467
and pork belly too.

01:32.550 --> 01:34.302
I wish they made perfumes out of them.

01:34.385 --> 01:36.596
Are you being optimistic or insane?

01:36.679 --> 01:38.097
Optimistically insane?

01:38.181 --> 01:39.182
I see.

01:40.058 --> 01:41.726
It's tough, right?

01:44.354 --> 01:45.355
Still,

01:46.773 --> 01:48.525
this is nothing compared to dinner time.

01:54.155 --> 01:55.281
Good luck.

02:05.875 --> 02:06.960
Good luck.

02:08.211 --> 02:10.547
Wait, are you leaving? Really?

02:12.632 --> 02:14.008
- Let me go.
- No way.

02:14.092 --> 02:15.552
Over my dead body.

02:15.635 --> 02:16.761
Let me go right now.

02:16.845 --> 02:19.848
No, I can't! I won't let you go!

02:19.931 --> 02:21.724
- Let me go.
- No.

02:21.808 --> 02:24.144
You and I are in the same boat today!

02:24.227 --> 02:26.271
Stop clinging to my pants!

02:26.354 --> 02:28.398
Then stop trying to leave.

02:28.481 --> 02:30.775
I won't go, so let go of my pants already!

02:30.859 --> 02:33.194
- Do you promise?
- I do. So just let go.

02:35.738 --> 02:36.823
Jeez.

02:38.741 --> 02:41.452
Look at you.
Already spending your part-time pay.

02:41.536 --> 02:44.789
The reason you're always broke
is because you buy these useless things.

02:45.331 --> 02:46.332
Hey.

02:47.083 --> 02:48.376
Let's go out this weekend.

02:48.459 --> 02:50.628
What is it this time?

02:50.712 --> 02:53.047
A part-time job cleaning corpses?

02:56.092 --> 02:57.093
That must pay a lot.

02:58.344 --> 03:00.763
- Why didn't I think of that sooner?
- What?

03:00.847 --> 03:02.390
Where can I get a job doing that?

03:02.974 --> 03:05.226
- This isn't what I expected.
- You're a genius!

03:05.768 --> 03:07.687
Why earn money
if you're going to waste it?

03:07.770 --> 03:09.230
In order to waste it, of course!

03:16.029 --> 03:17.030
What is this?

03:21.743 --> 03:22.744
I was right!

03:23.328 --> 03:25.955
I knew you'd find it first
if I hid it here.

03:26.456 --> 03:28.499
This is made of real gold, okay?

03:29.083 --> 03:30.209
Don't give it to anyone else.

03:34.088 --> 03:35.298
It's beautiful.

04:16.130 --> 04:22.428
HATE

04:46.369 --> 04:48.246
Onto the next news item.

04:48.913 --> 04:51.374
Many of you
will find this quite thrilling.

04:51.457 --> 04:55.420
This week brings
a spectacular cosmic event,

04:55.503 --> 04:59.048
the Eta Aquariids meteor shower.

04:59.716 --> 05:02.260
With the moon
in its waning crescent phase,

05:02.343 --> 05:05.555
its light will have minimal impact
on the visibility of the shower.

05:05.638 --> 05:06.889
However, please be aware

05:06.973 --> 05:09.600
that potential rain could impact
the visibility of the event.

05:09.684 --> 05:10.893
Come and eat.

05:10.977 --> 05:12.645
- If the weather is favorable--
- Okay.

05:13.438 --> 05:15.940
So should I…

05:16.566 --> 05:17.900
wake Seok-ryu up?

05:19.736 --> 05:22.155
Maybe I should just let her sleep, right?

05:23.156 --> 05:24.282
Hey.

05:26.951 --> 05:28.286
Good morning.

05:29.662 --> 05:30.663
Did you sleep well?

05:30.747 --> 05:32.290
I slept like a baby.

05:33.416 --> 05:34.417
What is this?

05:35.251 --> 05:37.962
You made gochujang stew, Mom?

05:39.422 --> 05:41.674
This smell makes it feel like
I'm truly back home.

05:41.758 --> 05:44.385
Right? Your mom's gochujang stew
is the best.

05:44.469 --> 05:45.636
Here you go.

05:45.720 --> 05:47.346
Why are there only three portions?

05:47.430 --> 05:49.557
Where's my bowl of rice, Mom?

05:49.640 --> 05:50.516
Honey.

05:51.267 --> 05:52.310
Mom.

05:53.394 --> 05:56.064
I see. She's pretending I don't exist.

05:56.147 --> 05:58.274
It's fine. I can get it on my own.

05:58.357 --> 05:59.817
Yes, good thinking.

06:01.778 --> 06:04.947
She's already so skinny as she is.
You should at least feed--

06:08.326 --> 06:10.078
I'm asking you one last time.

06:10.161 --> 06:11.996
Did you really mean everything you said

06:12.080 --> 06:13.164
last night?

06:15.208 --> 06:16.375
Tell me the truth.

06:16.459 --> 06:18.419
No matter how I look at it,

06:19.045 --> 06:22.465
I can't believe that you cheated.
You don't have it in you.

06:22.548 --> 06:23.591
How do you know?

06:23.674 --> 06:26.344
Maybe I have a whole other
seductress side of me.

06:26.427 --> 06:27.261
You little…

06:28.513 --> 06:30.431
I know you do outlandish things sometimes,

06:30.515 --> 06:32.558
but never something like this.

06:32.642 --> 06:34.310
You have a line you wouldn't cross.

06:34.393 --> 06:37.605
Right. You continued going to school
even after you ran away from home.

06:37.688 --> 06:41.526
There must be a valid reason
for your decision to end your engagement

06:42.110 --> 06:42.944
and quit your job.

06:43.903 --> 06:44.904
So tell me what it is.

06:46.155 --> 06:47.907
I just got bored.

06:47.990 --> 06:49.117
What?

06:49.200 --> 06:51.536
I worked in the same company
for too many years.

06:51.619 --> 06:53.663
I was fed up with it all.

06:53.746 --> 06:55.289
And then it got me thinking,

06:55.373 --> 06:58.251
"Wouldn't I eventually
get bored with my marriage too?"

06:58.334 --> 07:00.044
So I quit both of them.

07:00.128 --> 07:01.629
- Hey…
- Are you kidding me?

07:03.714 --> 07:07.760
So what are you planning to do now?

07:07.844 --> 07:10.972
You wouldn't have caused
such a commotion without a plan, right?

07:11.055 --> 07:13.349
- Of course not.
- Of course she has a plan!

07:13.432 --> 07:15.309
- The last letter of your MBTI is…
- J.

07:15.393 --> 07:18.521
So tell me what you're going to do now.

07:18.604 --> 07:19.480
First,

07:21.065 --> 07:22.483
- I'm going to sleep.
- What?

07:22.567 --> 07:24.569
- She's going to sleep.
- I'm turning off my alarm

07:25.153 --> 07:26.779
and sleeping for as long as I want.

07:26.863 --> 07:30.116
And I also want to eat
a lot of good Korean food.

07:30.199 --> 07:31.033
You…

07:35.913 --> 07:36.789
And then?

07:36.873 --> 07:37.957
And then…

07:39.000 --> 07:40.918
I just want to do nothing for a while.

07:41.794 --> 07:43.671
Is that your plan?

07:43.754 --> 07:44.589
Yes.

07:46.340 --> 07:48.134
I want to be happily unemployed.

07:52.180 --> 07:53.431
You stay out of it!

07:54.390 --> 07:56.100
- Were you serious?
- Yes.

07:56.184 --> 07:57.768
I was completely serious for real.

07:59.687 --> 08:01.063
You don't get to eat.

08:01.147 --> 08:03.441
You don't have the right to eat.

08:03.524 --> 08:06.152
You're being so harsh.

08:06.235 --> 08:07.862
You're all being so loud.

08:07.945 --> 08:10.114
- You woke me up.
- You little… Wake up earlier.

08:10.198 --> 08:12.950
What are you, a caveman? Wear something.

08:13.034 --> 08:15.161
This body is meant to be seen, not hidden.

08:16.746 --> 08:18.122
Eat your breakfast.

08:18.873 --> 08:20.082
Someone is here.

08:22.168 --> 08:25.004
- You go. I'm your older sister.
- See who it is.

08:26.339 --> 08:27.256
Who is it?

08:27.340 --> 08:28.966
- It's Seung-hyo.
- Is it?

08:29.050 --> 08:29.926
Well, let him in!

08:30.801 --> 08:31.802
Mo-eum is here too.

08:32.803 --> 08:34.889
- I'm touched.
- Get dressed, Dong-jin.

08:34.972 --> 08:36.724
- That's right.
- Okay.

08:36.807 --> 08:38.392
Cover yourself up.

08:39.894 --> 08:40.728
Hello.

08:40.811 --> 08:42.271
How are you, Auntie?

08:42.355 --> 08:43.648
- Welcome.
- Good morning.

08:43.731 --> 08:44.732
- What's all this?
- Morning.

08:45.316 --> 08:46.192
Look up.

08:47.068 --> 08:49.111
- Show me your tongue.
- Mo-eum.

08:49.195 --> 08:51.072
Your temperature
and blood pressure seem fine.

08:51.155 --> 08:51.989
Anything else?

08:52.073 --> 08:55.284
Were you worried
that I might've beaten her to death?

08:55.368 --> 08:59.455
Well, you almost did break her leg
when she ran away from home before.

08:59.539 --> 09:01.082
I should've gone through with it.

09:01.165 --> 09:03.042
- Come on.
- Did you get any sleep?

09:03.125 --> 09:04.335
What do you think?

09:04.418 --> 09:05.461
Of course you couldn't.

09:06.462 --> 09:09.173
I brought you some
of your favorite pumpkin porridge.

09:10.508 --> 09:12.385
You're the only one who takes care of me.

09:12.468 --> 09:14.971
What about me, Seung-hyo?
I passed out yesterday.

09:15.054 --> 09:16.138
Don't just stand about.

09:16.222 --> 09:17.932
You two didn't have breakfast, right?

09:18.015 --> 09:19.100
I didn't.

09:19.183 --> 09:21.686
I did, but I can always eat more.

09:22.478 --> 09:23.729
Hey, this is my seat.

09:23.813 --> 09:25.856
What a generous household this is.

09:26.482 --> 09:28.818
Starving the daughter to feed the guests.

09:28.901 --> 09:30.945
- Eat up. There's more.
- Okay.

09:31.028 --> 09:32.071
Give me your bowls.

09:32.154 --> 09:33.823
- The stew is cold.
- It's fine.

09:33.906 --> 09:35.449
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

09:39.912 --> 09:41.706
- That's right. Share.
- Thanks.

09:41.789 --> 09:43.040
Thank you for the meal.

09:43.124 --> 09:44.250
We need to talk.

09:44.333 --> 09:46.586
No, we don't.
I came here to see Aunt Mi-suk.

09:46.669 --> 09:49.130
Come have breakfast, Dong-jin!

09:49.213 --> 09:50.298
Don't make me serve it twice.

09:51.007 --> 09:51.882
I'm not eating.

09:53.759 --> 09:56.220
Consuming carbs is a crime,
and consuming sodium is a punishment.

09:56.929 --> 09:58.472
I can't get tempted by them.

09:58.556 --> 09:59.849
What a bunch of nonsense.

09:59.932 --> 10:02.768
Look, idiot. Tofu, kimchi,
seasoned vegetables, and meat.

10:03.311 --> 10:05.271
- It can't get any healthier than this.
- Here, honey.

10:05.354 --> 10:06.230
Thanks.

10:06.314 --> 10:09.025
You should know these things
if you want to be a trainer.

10:09.108 --> 10:10.443
Don't get on my nerves.

10:10.526 --> 10:13.529
This is why
you keep failing the certification exam.

10:14.113 --> 10:16.240
Look who's talking, you jobless pest.

10:16.824 --> 10:18.534
- Excuse me?
- There they go again.

10:19.535 --> 10:21.662
Did you just call me a pest?

10:21.746 --> 10:25.374
I'm sorry I hurt your feelings,
my pest of a sister.

10:25.458 --> 10:27.335
Did you just grab my hair bun, you brat?

10:27.418 --> 10:28.252
Let go.

10:28.336 --> 10:30.921
Not on my watch.
Get your hand off my head first, you pest.

10:31.005 --> 10:32.590
Let go, or else!

10:38.387 --> 10:39.764
Where are you going, Mom?

10:39.847 --> 10:42.308
That brute tore out my hair.

10:43.768 --> 10:44.810
Where's she going, Dad?

10:44.894 --> 10:45.895
You'll find out soon.

10:46.854 --> 10:47.688
Five,

10:47.772 --> 10:49.065
four,

10:49.148 --> 10:50.399
three,

10:50.983 --> 10:51.901
two,

10:51.984 --> 10:52.818
one.

11:04.538 --> 11:06.207
Is this coming from our basement?

11:06.290 --> 11:07.458
Yes.

11:07.541 --> 11:10.753
A legendary drummer lives in our basement.

11:11.253 --> 11:13.673
She only appears when her anger peaks.

11:14.840 --> 11:15.925
Is that drum kit

11:16.008 --> 11:18.386
the one you got in middle school
when you wanted to be a musician?

11:19.220 --> 11:20.513
Mom is so talented.

11:21.013 --> 11:22.723
She's good at anything
that involves hitting.

11:22.807 --> 11:23.641
She does.

11:24.225 --> 11:25.643
- She's really good.
- Yes.

11:25.726 --> 11:27.770
She's like Ringo Starr.

11:27.853 --> 11:31.232
She's as skilled at hitting those drums
as she is at hitting people.

11:46.455 --> 11:48.290
Come on, tell me already.

11:48.999 --> 11:50.000
What really happened?

11:52.670 --> 11:55.172
Why did you quit your job
and break off your engagement?

11:55.256 --> 11:56.757
You're rubbing it in.

11:57.299 --> 12:00.511
How could you rub salt in my wounds
when your job is to save people?

12:00.594 --> 12:03.305
You need to tell me so I can help you out.

12:03.389 --> 12:05.433
Why did you do it? Whose fault was it?

12:05.516 --> 12:07.560
Who, what, when, where, why, and how?

12:08.310 --> 12:10.062
Did my mom ask you to ask me?

12:11.647 --> 12:13.732
Yes. In the utility room.

12:13.816 --> 12:15.943
I'll let it go since you were honest.

12:16.026 --> 12:18.446
It just doesn't make any sense.

12:18.529 --> 12:21.782
It's not something
a perfectionist like you would do.

12:23.451 --> 12:24.785
A perfectionist?

12:25.369 --> 12:26.912
- Me?
- Yes.

12:26.996 --> 12:29.206
No one else I know
lives as diligently as you.

12:29.290 --> 12:32.209
Competitiveness, grit, drive,

12:32.293 --> 12:34.420
achievement, meticulousness,
and persistence.

12:34.503 --> 12:37.298
As I see it, you have it all.

12:37.381 --> 12:40.092
Do I? You flatter me too much.

12:40.926 --> 12:41.886
It wasn't a compliment.

12:42.636 --> 12:43.971
You're obsessed with success,

12:44.054 --> 12:45.931
neurotic about others' opinions,

12:46.015 --> 12:48.058
- and you have too much ambition--
- Hey!

12:48.142 --> 12:49.518
That's very accurate.

12:49.602 --> 12:51.395
So why would someone like you

12:51.479 --> 12:55.441
give up everything and come back here?

12:55.524 --> 12:56.734
Stuff happens, okay?

12:56.817 --> 12:58.194
Sure.

12:58.277 --> 13:00.362
To someone else, maybe.

13:00.446 --> 13:02.740
But not to you.

13:04.325 --> 13:05.326
Come on.

13:06.035 --> 13:08.162
Spit out the truth.

13:08.245 --> 13:09.914
- Come on.
- It's five minutes to nine.

13:09.997 --> 13:11.123
Tell me. What?

13:11.207 --> 13:12.124
You're late.

13:12.208 --> 13:13.584
- Go on.
- Darn it.

13:15.669 --> 13:17.213
- I'm not done with you.
- Bye.

13:17.296 --> 13:18.297
See you.

13:19.089 --> 13:21.509
If you keep lazing around like that,

13:21.592 --> 13:23.177
you'll go to the Hell of Indolence.

13:23.260 --> 13:25.679
I don't care. I'm in heaven right now.

13:25.763 --> 13:28.098
If this is what heaven is like,
I'd rather not go.

13:28.182 --> 13:29.099
How do you even sleep here?

13:29.183 --> 13:31.101
Come here for a second, Choisseung.

13:32.019 --> 13:33.395
- Why?
- I have something to say.

13:33.938 --> 13:34.855
Get up first.

13:34.939 --> 13:37.066
Just come here for a second!

13:37.149 --> 13:38.984
- I don't want to.
- Come on!

13:39.068 --> 13:41.654
It's important! Come on, hurry up!

13:41.737 --> 13:44.365
Stop throwing a tantrum, you nutcase.

13:45.074 --> 13:46.116
What is it now?

13:46.200 --> 13:47.493
Come closer.

13:48.077 --> 13:49.328
- Jeez.
- Hey.

13:49.411 --> 13:50.621
Wanna know something cool?

13:51.413 --> 13:52.915
You traitor.

13:52.998 --> 13:55.543
How could you
just hand me over to my mom like that?

13:55.626 --> 13:56.710
I'll end you today.

13:56.794 --> 13:58.295
I did it for you.

13:58.379 --> 14:00.297
You did it for me?

14:00.881 --> 14:01.924
Is that right?

14:02.007 --> 14:03.717
George Orwell once said,

14:03.801 --> 14:07.638
"The quickest way of ending a war
is to lose it."

14:07.721 --> 14:10.307
Bae Seok-ryu once said,

14:10.391 --> 14:12.810
"A traitor must be punished by death."

14:12.893 --> 14:14.687
I can't breathe. Aunt Mi-suk!

14:14.770 --> 14:15.980
What's going on?

14:16.063 --> 14:18.190
- Take that, you jerk.
- You little brat! What are you doing?

14:18.274 --> 14:20.317
- It hurts.
- My goodness.

14:20.401 --> 14:22.069
Are you okay, Seung-hyo?

14:22.152 --> 14:23.237
- Auntie.
- You're nuts!

14:23.320 --> 14:24.697
She tried to kill me.

14:24.780 --> 14:26.574
Dear me.

14:27.157 --> 14:29.076
- Are you hurt?
- I'm fine.

14:29.159 --> 14:32.496
Judging by the way you coddle him,
you'd think he's your actual son.

14:32.580 --> 14:33.914
If only that was the case!

14:33.998 --> 14:36.041
Yeah? Then why don't you
exchange me for him?

14:36.125 --> 14:39.587
There's an idea. Should I be your son
from now on, Aunt Mi-suk?

14:40.296 --> 14:42.423
I'm all for it. But what about work?

14:42.506 --> 14:43.549
I have to go now.

14:44.550 --> 14:45.426
It hurts.

14:45.926 --> 14:47.553
Hey, get up.

14:47.636 --> 14:49.513
You didn't have to kick me.

14:49.597 --> 14:51.891
You should be grateful
I didn't trample you to death!

14:51.974 --> 14:53.642
You're so mean to me, Mom.

14:53.726 --> 14:54.560
Shut it.

14:54.643 --> 14:57.438
Get up and take these rice cakes
to Seung-hyo's office.

14:57.521 --> 14:59.398
Tell him to do it himself!

14:59.481 --> 15:00.357
- Rice cakes?
- Yes.

15:00.441 --> 15:03.277
I ordered some rice cakes for you.

15:03.360 --> 15:06.071
You should hand them out
to everyone in the neighborhood.

15:06.155 --> 15:08.866
You take such good care of me. Thank you.

15:09.366 --> 15:10.659
How touching.

15:10.743 --> 15:13.287
You're moving me to tears.

15:13.370 --> 15:14.204
Get up!

15:16.081 --> 15:17.166
He looks so handsome.

15:17.249 --> 15:18.167
Na-yun!

15:19.209 --> 15:22.963
So the client from Buryeong-dong
wants the windows somewhere else?

15:23.047 --> 15:26.884
Yes. Initially, he wanted them
oriented east for the morning sun.

15:27.676 --> 15:30.054
But now he wants to see sunsets instead.

15:30.137 --> 15:32.306
Why does he keep changing his mind?

15:32.389 --> 15:33.641
We already started construction!

15:34.391 --> 15:38.020
Hey, I called you in
to organize the desks,

15:38.103 --> 15:40.439
but here you are,
organizing Seung-hyo's photos instead.

15:41.315 --> 15:42.274
- Myeong-u.
- Hey.

15:42.358 --> 15:43.901
What did the Buryeong-dong client say?

15:43.984 --> 15:45.152
He said…

15:45.235 --> 15:47.154
Oh, is she a new client?

15:47.237 --> 15:49.865
- Hello, welcome.
- Hello.

15:50.532 --> 15:51.909
What is this?

15:55.079 --> 15:56.872
I'm sorry.

15:56.956 --> 16:00.209
You'll have to wait a bit
since Seung-hyo's on the phone.

16:00.292 --> 16:03.003
Don't worry about it.
I just came to deliver the rice cakes.

16:03.087 --> 16:06.465
You even brought us rice cakes.
We should at least serve you some tea.

16:06.548 --> 16:09.885
These are from my mom.
I'm just delivering them.

16:11.136 --> 16:13.681
Wait, are you…

16:13.764 --> 16:16.558
the childhood friend
that Seung-hyo told me about?

16:16.642 --> 16:18.060
Yes, I am. Do you know me?

16:18.143 --> 16:22.147
Of course I do!
I'm thrilled to finally meet you.

16:22.731 --> 16:24.441
- That's right. Next Tuesday,
- Yes?

16:24.525 --> 16:26.610
we're hosting an opening party.

16:26.694 --> 16:28.112
You should come.

16:28.195 --> 16:29.613
Oh, okay.

16:30.155 --> 16:31.365
Drink up.

16:31.949 --> 16:33.617
So you've known Seung-hyo for a long time?

16:33.701 --> 16:36.328
I guess we have a long history.

16:36.412 --> 16:38.122
Please enlighten me.

16:38.205 --> 16:40.249
I want to know everything chronologically.

16:40.332 --> 16:43.043
- Well, let's see.
- Don't.

16:43.127 --> 16:44.503
It's going to be very long.

16:46.213 --> 16:48.257
You know he was born in France, right?

16:48.340 --> 16:49.174
Yes.

16:50.259 --> 16:52.553
It all started in 1995.

16:53.262 --> 16:55.097
A summer's day

16:55.180 --> 16:58.267
when the playground dirt
was as hot as coal.

16:59.435 --> 17:01.270
- Bonjour.
- Seung-hyo.

17:01.353 --> 17:04.648
It was a day like any other.
I came home from playing outside

17:04.732 --> 17:06.775
and found a boy
standing in front of my house.

17:06.859 --> 17:08.527
That was Seung-hyo.

17:08.610 --> 17:10.571
- Get along, okay?
- Okay.

17:10.654 --> 17:11.822
Say hello, Seung-hyo.

17:12.406 --> 17:13.907
Hi. What's your name?

17:13.991 --> 17:17.077
He was so short
and couldn't speak any Korean either.

17:17.161 --> 17:19.621
He kept hiding behind his mother.

17:19.705 --> 17:21.415
That was when it hit me.

17:21.498 --> 17:22.416
Say hello.

17:22.499 --> 17:25.544
I'd have to help this fragile boy out.

17:25.627 --> 17:26.545
I'll leave him in your care.

17:26.628 --> 17:27.880
Don't worry about a thing.

17:27.963 --> 17:30.049
Aunt Hye-suk left Seung-hyo in our care

17:30.132 --> 17:32.301
when she began working
at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs

17:32.384 --> 17:33.635
because my mom

17:33.719 --> 17:35.763
- used to work as a babysitter.
- Welcome.

17:35.846 --> 17:37.056
You're so cute.

17:37.639 --> 17:39.224
- She's a cutie.
- You little brat.

17:39.308 --> 17:41.894
That was when I started looking after him.

17:41.977 --> 17:43.896
Does my baby
want to be a king or a prince?

17:43.979 --> 17:45.064
No, wait.

17:45.647 --> 17:47.149
You should be a princess.

17:47.232 --> 17:48.484
All of this is your castle.

17:48.567 --> 17:51.236
I engaged him in creative play.

17:51.320 --> 17:52.196
It's huge, right?

17:52.780 --> 17:55.199
Do you need to pee, baby?

17:56.450 --> 18:00.120
I protected his dignity as a toddler
and took care of his hygiene.

18:01.747 --> 18:03.582
This will make you grow taller.

18:03.665 --> 18:06.251
And this will make your teeth stronger.

18:06.335 --> 18:10.005
I also encouraged healthy eating habits
so he could get proper nutrition.

18:10.089 --> 18:11.465
This one is just good for you.

18:12.049 --> 18:13.467
Eat up, my baby.

18:17.679 --> 18:18.931
Everyone, be nice to him.

18:19.431 --> 18:20.641
You don't have a problem with that,

18:21.683 --> 18:22.518
right?

18:23.560 --> 18:26.522
I contributed to his social development
within his peer group.

18:29.024 --> 18:30.692
Yes, I believe we have enough.

18:31.610 --> 18:32.444
Let's go, baby.

18:32.528 --> 18:34.822
I even helped him learn about economics.

18:36.281 --> 18:40.244
I basically raised Seung-hyo.

18:42.287 --> 18:43.539
That's just what you think.

18:46.875 --> 18:50.003
Don't come to my workplace
and spread rumors about me.

18:50.087 --> 18:52.214
I should sue you
for spreading false information.

18:52.297 --> 18:54.675
What an ungrateful jerk.

18:54.758 --> 18:57.010
You should repay me instead of suing me!

18:57.094 --> 18:58.095
She's right.

18:58.178 --> 19:01.056
Don't trust her.
Every word she says is a lie.

19:01.140 --> 19:02.975
She's a compulsive liar.

19:03.058 --> 19:05.811
No way.
Her story doesn't sound like a lie.

19:05.894 --> 19:07.354
It has a narrative arc.

19:07.437 --> 19:09.481
- Yes, it does.
- Yes.

19:09.565 --> 19:10.774
But it's been manipulated.

19:11.483 --> 19:12.484
This girl

19:13.569 --> 19:16.655
was the first lunatic I met in my life.

19:16.738 --> 19:17.573
Lunatic?

19:17.656 --> 19:21.118
Seung-hyo, she's my old friend, Mi-suk.

19:21.201 --> 19:24.079
And that girl is her daughter, Seok-ryu.

19:24.163 --> 19:25.372
She's the same age as you.

19:27.541 --> 19:29.459
Hi. What's your name?

19:30.794 --> 19:32.087
You're dirty.

19:32.754 --> 19:34.840
I could tell since our first encounter.

19:34.923 --> 19:36.383
- Hi, Seok-ryu.
- Hello!

19:36.967 --> 19:38.218
She was so aggressive.

19:38.302 --> 19:39.469
You're so cute.

19:39.553 --> 19:40.679
It was overwhelming.

19:40.762 --> 19:42.389
Gross.

19:46.476 --> 19:48.437
Does my baby
want to be a king or a prince?

19:48.979 --> 19:50.480
You both know me.

19:50.564 --> 19:51.940
I need my alone time.

19:52.024 --> 19:53.358
It's sticky.

19:54.860 --> 19:55.861
But this girl

19:55.944 --> 19:58.071
- All of this is your castle.
- never left me alone.

19:58.155 --> 19:59.781
It's so big!

19:59.865 --> 20:02.451
She disrupted my peaceful solitude.

20:03.202 --> 20:04.620
Do you need to pee, baby?

20:12.961 --> 20:13.962
Hey!

20:14.046 --> 20:16.506
- She sexually harassed me,
- Mom! He's speaking Korean!

20:16.590 --> 20:18.425
leaving me no choice but to speak up.

20:18.508 --> 20:20.761
- I hate beans in rice.
- And she says she taught me Korean.

20:23.305 --> 20:24.139
Here.

20:24.806 --> 20:26.016
Eat some beans, Seung-hyo.

20:27.059 --> 20:30.062
She gave me things
that she didn't want to eat.

20:30.145 --> 20:31.146
I don't like them.

20:32.439 --> 20:34.233
A baby shouldn't be picky.

20:34.816 --> 20:36.318
Eat up, my baby.

20:36.818 --> 20:37.986
Who's going to be "it"?

20:38.570 --> 20:39.655
My baby.

20:40.489 --> 20:41.740
He'll do it.

20:41.823 --> 20:43.617
- Red light, green light.
- Baby should be "it."

20:43.700 --> 20:44.743
Red light…

20:44.826 --> 20:46.286
She told everyone to be nice,

20:46.370 --> 20:48.205
but made me be "it" all the time.

20:54.962 --> 20:56.380
Let's go, baby.

20:56.463 --> 20:59.508
That's right. She even began
stealing my money later on.

20:59.591 --> 21:00.676
I'll get my revenge.

21:02.177 --> 21:03.262
All my allowance

21:03.762 --> 21:05.639
turned into chocolates and ice creams

21:05.722 --> 21:07.808
and ended up in that mouth right there.

21:07.891 --> 21:10.477
Says the boy who couldn't even
use the toilet on his own.

21:10.560 --> 21:14.189
You're the little pervert
who followed me into the bathroom.

21:14.273 --> 21:15.607
I was trying to help you.

21:15.691 --> 21:17.192
You couldn't unzip your pants

21:17.276 --> 21:18.986
- and kept wetting yourself.
- Goodness.

21:19.069 --> 21:21.321
Stop spewing such nonsense.

21:21.405 --> 21:23.448
I told you,
some water splashed onto my pants.

21:23.532 --> 21:24.908
It didn't look like water.

21:25.534 --> 21:26.576
Oh dear.

21:27.160 --> 21:28.328
My goodness.

21:29.329 --> 21:32.582
I've never seen Seung-hyo
act so childish before.

21:32.666 --> 21:36.169
Me neither. But seeing how they even
went to the bathroom together,

21:36.253 --> 21:38.130
I can tell they're really close friends.

21:38.755 --> 21:41.717
You know, I've been reading
various romance stories for ten years

21:41.800 --> 21:43.927
- from fanfics to fantasy novels.
- Yeah?

21:44.011 --> 21:46.305
And there's one trope I get crazy over.

21:47.055 --> 21:48.974
The one and only childhood friend trope.

21:49.516 --> 21:50.517
What's that supposed to mean?

21:52.060 --> 21:53.895
They should start looking for
English kindergartens for their kids.

21:54.438 --> 21:56.773
Do you have any idea
how expensive English kindergartens are?

21:56.857 --> 22:00.193
And yet my wife
wants our twins to enroll in one!

22:01.278 --> 22:03.655
Hey, where are you going? I'm not done!

22:06.950 --> 22:08.160
This is Yoon Myeong-u.

22:08.243 --> 22:09.244
Oh, hello.

22:10.829 --> 22:11.997
Excuse me?

22:16.710 --> 22:18.295
- Did you hear?
- What?

22:18.378 --> 22:21.214
Apparently, Root Diner's daughter
cheated on her fiancé,

22:21.298 --> 22:22.424
so the engagement's off.

22:22.507 --> 22:26.303
Of course I heard about that.
Everyone knows already!

22:26.386 --> 22:28.513
- I knew it.
- Oh my.

22:28.597 --> 22:31.558
Didn't Mi-suk brag
about her daughter's great job in the US?

22:31.641 --> 22:34.895
I heard she got fired too.
That'll teach her not to brag so much.

22:34.978 --> 22:36.480
I know, right?

22:37.814 --> 22:41.234
Did you go grocery shopping, Mi-suk?

22:41.318 --> 22:43.820
Yes. I wanted to shred something.

22:45.822 --> 22:47.616
What are you going to shred?

22:48.241 --> 22:50.660
I haven't decided yet.
It could be some vegetables

22:50.744 --> 22:52.954
or someone unlucky.

23:00.212 --> 23:02.089
HYEREUNG REALTY

23:04.049 --> 23:05.133
Hey, Mi-suk.

23:05.217 --> 23:08.011
All right, Hye-suk. Okay.

23:08.095 --> 23:10.972
I'll see what I can do. All right.

23:11.056 --> 23:13.517
Goodbye.

23:16.061 --> 23:17.145
Oh my.

23:17.229 --> 23:19.439
Why is your face so red?

23:19.523 --> 23:20.524
Those darn gossipers.

23:21.024 --> 23:22.859
They're having a field day.

23:22.943 --> 23:26.071
They were absolutely going at it
behind my back!

23:26.154 --> 23:27.614
They're the worst.

23:27.697 --> 23:28.990
If you didn't want that to happen,

23:29.074 --> 23:32.327
you shouldn't have beat up your daughter
in front of everyone…

23:32.410 --> 23:34.412
What I mean is,

23:34.496 --> 23:39.334
it would've been better to discipline her
in the privacy of your own home.

23:41.795 --> 23:42.921
What did Hye-suk say?

23:43.004 --> 23:46.091
Actually, she told me
she invited the Hee Sisters

23:46.174 --> 23:47.884
to Seung-hyo's opening party.

23:47.968 --> 23:49.469
You mean Yeong-hee, Soon-hee,
Jung-hee, and Min-hee?

23:49.553 --> 23:51.972
- Yes, them.
- Why would she invite those snooty girls?

23:52.055 --> 23:55.100
Don't you remember Hye-suk telling them
about Seung-hyo's new office

23:55.183 --> 23:56.143
at the class reunion?

23:57.018 --> 24:00.105
Why did she blab about it
to people she's not even close to?

24:00.188 --> 24:03.024
"Oh dear, didn't you guys know?"

24:03.108 --> 24:05.360
"My daughter works for Greip."

24:05.944 --> 24:07.612
"She's getting married too,

24:07.696 --> 24:09.739
and the wedding will be held in the US."

24:09.823 --> 24:12.784
"My son-in-law
is an international lawyer."

24:13.869 --> 24:15.829
It's humid as hell today.

24:15.912 --> 24:18.165
Also, I never spoke that smugly.

24:18.248 --> 24:20.500
"International lawyer. Greip."

24:21.084 --> 24:22.502
- "International lawyer…"
- This is so annoying.

24:22.586 --> 24:24.629
- That's enough!
- Jeez, calm down.

24:28.550 --> 24:31.636
Sunsets in Korea are the best.

25:06.087 --> 25:07.088
It's done.

25:24.940 --> 25:27.567
Bravo! What was that cool trick just now?

25:28.568 --> 25:29.569
It's nothing.

25:29.653 --> 25:31.655
Just a survival tactic I learned abroad.

25:31.738 --> 25:34.032
Oh, I see.

25:34.115 --> 25:35.158
Where's Seung-hyo?

25:35.242 --> 25:36.660
Why would I call that jerk?

25:37.285 --> 25:38.536
Where are you, Seung-hyo?

25:38.620 --> 25:39.829
Don't call him over!

25:39.913 --> 25:41.539
Come to Seok-ryu's if you're done.

25:42.624 --> 25:44.584
What do you mean "why"?
Have dinner with us.

25:45.085 --> 25:46.628
Okay, bye.

25:47.420 --> 25:48.255
Is he coming?

25:48.338 --> 25:50.840
No, he told us to stuff our faces
without him.

25:51.591 --> 25:52.801
Seok-ryu.

25:53.385 --> 25:54.803
Do you have anything to drink?

25:54.886 --> 25:55.762
I don't.

25:56.263 --> 25:59.432
We have better soju at home.

25:59.516 --> 26:01.518
I need that for the diner.

26:06.231 --> 26:08.108
I don't want to see Seok-ryu's face.

26:08.191 --> 26:09.150
Really?

26:09.943 --> 26:12.195
I like that she's back home.

26:13.571 --> 26:14.406
Seriously?

26:15.156 --> 26:17.951
Do you also like seeing her
sprawled around doing nothing?

26:19.411 --> 26:21.371
My blood is boiling
just thinking about it.

26:21.454 --> 26:24.082
I also feel like
I've been through a hurricane.

26:24.165 --> 26:27.711
My heart is in pieces
like it's been hit by a natural disaster.

26:27.794 --> 26:31.798
Then why don't you
have a talk with Seok-ryu?

26:31.881 --> 26:33.717
I bet she's hiding something from us.

26:33.800 --> 26:35.927
Get her to tell you the rest.

26:36.011 --> 26:39.264
Just leave her alone. What's with you?

26:39.347 --> 26:42.809
How could you be so indifferent?
It's like she's a stranger to you.

26:42.892 --> 26:44.561
You're acting as if
she's not your daughter.

26:44.644 --> 26:46.187
That's out of line!

26:46.271 --> 26:47.522
I'm just saying.

26:48.398 --> 26:50.775
You're so carefree, sitting on your hands,

26:50.859 --> 26:52.694
while I feel like I'm on a razor's edge.

26:56.114 --> 26:57.741
There you go, being silent again.

26:58.325 --> 27:01.202
You're avoiding the problem
just like you always do.

27:11.338 --> 27:12.756
I'm too scared to ask.

27:13.965 --> 27:15.925
I'm afraid her engagement broke off

27:17.427 --> 27:19.346
because I wasn't good enough
for her fiancé's family.

27:27.979 --> 27:28.938
That was so cool.

27:29.022 --> 27:30.815
- I'm so good at it, right?
- You are!

27:30.899 --> 27:32.108
- Aren't I awesome?
- You are.

27:32.192 --> 27:33.568
It was like watching a circus.

27:33.651 --> 27:34.778
That was a hard one.

27:34.861 --> 27:35.820
- It looked hard.
- Right?

27:35.904 --> 27:37.614
Come on, show me again!

27:37.697 --> 27:41.076
You guys are too loud.
I could hear you down the street.

27:41.159 --> 27:43.328
- Hi.
- Look at this party crasher.

27:43.411 --> 27:44.496
You ruined the mood.

27:44.579 --> 27:46.623
Shoo!

27:46.706 --> 27:48.041
Did you buy something to drink?

27:48.124 --> 27:49.084
Of course not.

27:49.834 --> 27:51.920
You guys don't know how to have fun.

27:52.003 --> 27:57.008
Listen. We really need some beer
on a lovely spring night like this.

27:57.717 --> 27:59.260
- Should I go buy some?
- Never mind.

27:59.803 --> 28:00.637
I'll go.

28:01.596 --> 28:02.472
Thanks.

28:03.056 --> 28:05.850
Or should I get rice wine
to go with the green onion pancakes?

28:05.934 --> 28:06.976
Beer for me.

28:07.060 --> 28:08.019
Zip it.

28:10.397 --> 28:14.317
Aren't you too busy
to be here or something?

28:14.401 --> 28:16.444
- Are you picking a fight already?
- No, I mean…

28:17.404 --> 28:19.239
It looked kind of serious earlier.

28:20.198 --> 28:23.159
If you're going to keep lying,
just go home.

28:23.243 --> 28:24.953
Why did you come here anyway?

28:25.036 --> 28:26.496
Watch your mouth.

28:26.579 --> 28:28.248
I carried these all the way here.

28:28.331 --> 28:30.125
- You should be grateful.
- Seung-hyo!

28:30.708 --> 28:32.919
I mean, Mr. Choi. We need to talk.

28:38.675 --> 28:41.344
The townhouse project is being delayed?
Why so suddenly?

28:41.428 --> 28:43.722
Due to the increase in raw materials costs
and construction costs.

28:43.805 --> 28:45.223
It's been suspended indefinitely.

28:45.306 --> 28:48.351
Then they won't pay us for the designs
until construction resumes.

28:48.435 --> 28:51.229
What do we do?
We still have a lot of expenses to cover.

28:52.480 --> 28:55.692
We'll get paid for
the youth center in Seongjin though.

28:55.775 --> 28:58.778
They said they'll pay us next year
because of budget issues.

28:58.862 --> 29:00.530
The economy must be really bad.

29:00.613 --> 29:02.615
We don't have any new clients either.

29:05.577 --> 29:06.828
Something happened, right?

29:06.911 --> 29:08.455
Something's happening right there.

29:09.122 --> 29:10.665
- It's burning.
- Oh no.

29:14.169 --> 29:15.462
Damn it, it's burnt.

29:21.593 --> 29:23.511
I'm glad if it's nothing to worry about.

29:24.012 --> 29:24.929
Do you want some?

29:25.013 --> 29:26.931
You want me to eat that?

29:27.015 --> 29:28.975
No, I'll make you another one.

29:29.058 --> 29:31.394
Move over. I'll make my own.

29:31.478 --> 29:32.687
No way.

29:32.771 --> 29:34.606
You just hurt my pride.

29:34.689 --> 29:37.317
I'll have you know
that I'm known as House Cook Master Bae.

29:37.859 --> 29:42.113
I even had a vlog channel
specializing in Korean cooking.

29:43.239 --> 29:44.240
I see.

29:45.408 --> 29:46.659
You don't believe me?

29:48.036 --> 29:49.412
I'll show it to you.

29:50.663 --> 29:52.540
How long are you going to hold out?

29:55.126 --> 29:57.629
You managed to hold them off for two days,

29:58.338 --> 30:00.340
but your parents and Mo-eum
will keep asking

30:01.007 --> 30:02.842
why you did what you did.

30:03.635 --> 30:04.803
They won't stop asking.

30:06.930 --> 30:07.931
What about you?

30:10.350 --> 30:11.309
Are you going to ask?

30:14.896 --> 30:15.897
I'm not curious.

30:17.690 --> 30:20.026
Hey, I don't care.

30:20.777 --> 30:22.612
I'll never tell you anyway,

30:22.695 --> 30:24.906
even if I tell everyone else in the world.

30:25.824 --> 30:26.741
Fine.

30:30.495 --> 30:31.663
But still,

30:32.580 --> 30:35.416
you shouldn't wait too long
to tell Aunt Mi-suk.

30:38.837 --> 30:39.838
She's your mother.

30:54.894 --> 30:55.770
What is it?

30:56.354 --> 30:57.647
Did Mom ask you to do this?

30:58.356 --> 30:59.190
What?

31:00.650 --> 31:01.985
- Hey.
- You little rat.

31:02.068 --> 31:03.945
Get ready for round two.

31:04.028 --> 31:06.239
Let go of me, you nutcase.

31:06.322 --> 31:07.699
I told you not to let your guard down.

31:07.782 --> 31:08.950
Come on, it really hurts.

31:09.951 --> 31:12.036
- Wait, I'm…
- You punk.

31:14.289 --> 31:15.790
It really hurts.

31:21.087 --> 31:23.464
MY SON-IN-LAW

31:38.313 --> 31:39.439
He's not picking up.

31:43.776 --> 31:44.903
Why are you hiding your phone?

31:45.612 --> 31:46.654
Who were you calling?

31:49.741 --> 31:51.075
I guess she can't hear me.

31:54.662 --> 31:57.498
Your ears aren't
failing already, are they?

31:59.709 --> 32:03.588
Are you going to
Choisseung's opening party tomorrow?

32:03.671 --> 32:04.756
Of course.

32:07.216 --> 32:09.552
Wait, are you going too?

32:09.636 --> 32:10.887
I was invited, so…

32:14.098 --> 32:16.476
No. Why would I go there?

32:17.769 --> 32:20.229
It's only been a few days,
but I'm already sick of him.

32:20.313 --> 32:22.899
Seung-hyo's like that, you know?

32:24.317 --> 32:27.070
- Hey, what are you doing?
- What were you trying to hide?

32:27.153 --> 32:29.197
Give it back now!

32:31.407 --> 32:32.450
Mom.

32:33.242 --> 32:34.410
Did you call him?

32:34.494 --> 32:35.703
Yes.

32:36.454 --> 32:38.623
What? Did I do something wrong?

32:38.706 --> 32:41.876
I told you we were over, Mom!

32:41.960 --> 32:43.503
You're not telling me everything,

32:43.586 --> 32:45.672
so I was going to ask him about it.

32:46.297 --> 32:48.091
What are you doing? Hey, stop!

32:49.008 --> 32:50.635
Don't call him ever again.

32:51.427 --> 32:52.637
You little…

32:53.930 --> 32:54.889
What the…

32:56.015 --> 32:58.393
Did she erase his number? My goodness.

33:01.813 --> 33:03.564
Do I really have to do this interview?

33:04.107 --> 33:06.067
It's not for promo. I know you hate those.

33:06.150 --> 33:07.568
It's a special on Social Overhead Capital.

33:07.652 --> 33:11.239
A reporter wanted to ask us
about the senior center we built.

33:12.156 --> 33:12.991
Is that so?

33:13.658 --> 33:15.243
What are you reading anyway?

33:15.994 --> 33:17.286
I'm researching precedents.

33:17.370 --> 33:19.831
It's not right
that they're not paying us the design fee.

33:20.748 --> 33:21.958
I'll ask around

33:22.041 --> 33:23.584
and meet up with a lawyer I know.

33:24.168 --> 33:25.378
Would that help?

33:27.005 --> 33:30.842
The contract doesn't specify
when the design fee has to be paid.

33:30.925 --> 33:32.343
Still, I should try everything.

33:33.094 --> 33:35.304
I'm worried about the loans too.

33:36.472 --> 33:37.306
Seung-hyo.

33:38.099 --> 33:40.643
Were we being rash
by building our own office?

33:42.103 --> 33:42.937
Wait.

33:43.646 --> 33:45.189
I think that's the reporter.

33:46.107 --> 33:47.692
He's going in the wrong direction.

33:49.027 --> 33:49.902
What…

33:51.821 --> 33:53.072
It's dangerous here, ma'am.

33:53.156 --> 33:54.866
I have to pick these up.

33:54.949 --> 33:56.659
It's such a waste.

33:56.743 --> 33:57.994
Let me. Please wait over there.

34:01.080 --> 34:02.040
Wait here, ma'am.

34:03.791 --> 34:04.876
I'm sorry.

34:08.337 --> 34:09.338
Thank you.

34:12.008 --> 34:13.593
Mr. Choi Seung-hyo?

34:13.676 --> 34:14.677
Let's hurry.

34:15.678 --> 34:16.596
Oh, right.

34:20.975 --> 34:21.976
Goodness.

34:23.352 --> 34:26.564
The wheels are worn out
and the axle is crooked.

34:26.647 --> 34:29.567
I managed to balance it for now,
but it won't last long.

34:30.234 --> 34:32.028
Where were you going?

34:32.111 --> 34:33.821
I'm taking them to a junkyard.

34:35.114 --> 34:37.450
How much can you sell them for?

34:37.533 --> 34:41.287
I used to get at least 130 won for 1 kg,

34:41.954 --> 34:43.664
but now I only get less than 100 won.

34:46.209 --> 34:50.088
I stole too much of your time.

34:50.171 --> 34:51.631
Thank you for your help.

34:52.590 --> 34:55.176
Will you be okay
with pulling this by yourself?

34:55.259 --> 34:57.804
I'll be fine. I do this every day.

34:59.764 --> 35:01.307
Then please be careful, ma'am.

35:02.058 --> 35:03.434
Let's go and do our interview.

35:04.602 --> 35:05.895
Do you want to push or pull?

35:07.271 --> 35:08.439
I'll push.

35:11.526 --> 35:13.152
We'll help you out.

35:14.445 --> 35:15.446
- Ready?
- Yes.

35:22.995 --> 35:24.956
Why aren't they coming?

35:33.673 --> 35:34.966
It's utterly unbelievable.

35:35.550 --> 35:36.384
Sorry?

35:36.884 --> 35:39.720
Oh, do you want some water?
I thought you didn't want any.

35:39.804 --> 35:41.305
I'm not talking about that.

35:41.389 --> 35:44.100
She only got 3,000 won
for that much cardboard and paper.

35:46.394 --> 35:47.395
I know, right?

35:48.354 --> 35:50.231
It was hard enough for two grown men.

35:50.940 --> 35:52.358
How does she do it every day?

35:53.734 --> 35:55.820
Life is tough.

36:46.662 --> 36:47.663
Hyeon-jun.

36:53.753 --> 36:54.837
I really…

36:57.465 --> 37:00.218
I really need you right now.

37:05.056 --> 37:06.182
Hyeon-jun.

37:37.797 --> 37:38.965
It's the last stop.

37:39.048 --> 37:40.007
Please get off.

37:42.718 --> 37:43.719
Oh, sorry.

37:47.431 --> 37:48.432
Thank you, sir.

37:48.516 --> 37:49.517
No problem.

37:55.606 --> 37:56.607
Hello, sir.

38:05.950 --> 38:09.078
The two of you used to work
at Jangyu Architecture, right?

38:09.161 --> 38:13.165
It's the best architecture firm in Korea,
not to mention ranking eleventh worldwide.

38:13.833 --> 38:16.294
May I ask
why you chose to branch out so early?

38:18.879 --> 38:21.966
I learned the basic principles
of architecture at Jangyu.

38:22.049 --> 38:25.928
They taught me everything I needed to know
to make a living.

38:26.846 --> 38:30.558
But since it's a huge company
that is departmentalized,

38:31.058 --> 38:33.561
some parts were out of my hands.

38:33.644 --> 38:35.062
You're right.

38:35.146 --> 38:36.480
The more I gained experience,

38:36.564 --> 38:39.900
the more I wanted to try
handling the projects by myself,

38:40.443 --> 38:42.486
from start to finish.

38:42.570 --> 38:46.157
It seems like you've achieved success
in a highly competitive field,

38:46.240 --> 38:48.576
with your own architectural firm
opening soon.

38:49.410 --> 38:50.703
How does it feel?

38:50.786 --> 38:52.538
To be honest, I'm regretting it.

38:53.205 --> 38:54.040
Sorry?

38:54.999 --> 38:57.335
What are you talking about?

38:58.169 --> 39:01.088
I doubt my decision a dozen times a day

39:01.172 --> 39:03.215
and wonder if I've made the right choice.

39:03.299 --> 39:05.593
But I still think that it's better

39:06.093 --> 39:09.305
to regret doing something
than to regret not doing something.

39:14.518 --> 39:16.187
I'm sorry. I have to take this.

39:16.270 --> 39:17.521
No worries.

39:21.150 --> 39:23.361
There's no hidden meaning behind it.

39:36.248 --> 39:38.209
When will you be back?

39:40.628 --> 39:41.670
The day after tomorrow.

39:42.254 --> 39:43.881
I'm on duty, and I have a seminar too.

39:43.964 --> 39:46.217
Did you forget
about Seung-hyo's opening ceremony?

39:46.300 --> 39:48.260
You should've cleared your schedule.

39:48.344 --> 39:49.345
I had no other choice.

39:50.096 --> 39:52.640
I'll send him flowers and give him a call.

39:54.266 --> 39:55.101
Do whatever you want.

39:59.563 --> 40:00.981
When is your next assignment?

40:01.816 --> 40:03.692
It's been a month since you returned
from Tunisia--

40:03.776 --> 40:05.152
It'll happen when it happens.

40:05.236 --> 40:07.446
Why? Do you want to get rid of me already?

40:08.030 --> 40:09.490
Tell me when you know for sure.

40:42.815 --> 40:45.693
POMEGRANATE TREE

40:50.948 --> 40:52.074
What are you doing here?

40:53.117 --> 40:54.827
Why are you home so late?

40:54.910 --> 40:56.370
I asked you first.

40:56.454 --> 40:57.663
Get some sleep.

40:58.706 --> 40:59.540
Hey!

41:00.749 --> 41:01.584
What?

41:03.002 --> 41:04.003
Take this.

41:08.674 --> 41:10.092
A pomegranate tree?

41:10.176 --> 41:11.427
For the opening ceremony tomorrow.

41:12.178 --> 41:13.637
I wanted to get you something unique.

41:13.721 --> 41:15.181
There, it'll remind you of me.

41:16.015 --> 41:16.932
Can I throw it away?

41:17.016 --> 41:18.476
Yes, you can throw it away,

41:19.101 --> 41:21.020
but pomegranates symbolize abundance.

41:21.103 --> 41:25.774
With every leaf that falls out,
your company will shrivel up too.

41:25.858 --> 41:28.194
So you were trying to curse me.
Take it back.

41:28.277 --> 41:30.529
You can't give back a present. Keep it.

41:30.613 --> 41:33.657
Just bring it with you tomorrow.
It's too heavy.

41:34.241 --> 41:35.409
I'm not going tomorrow.

41:36.285 --> 41:38.287
Why? Are you busy?

41:38.370 --> 41:39.914
Yes. Terribly busy.

41:40.623 --> 41:42.374
Say hello to Mr. Yoon for me.

41:57.223 --> 41:58.766
Where is it?

41:58.849 --> 42:01.101
I know I put it somewhere around here.

42:02.686 --> 42:05.022
What are you looking for?
You're going to be late.

42:05.105 --> 42:06.565
My brooch.

42:06.649 --> 42:09.860
The one you bought me a long time ago
with a pearl in the middle.

42:09.944 --> 42:11.195
Oh, that?

42:11.820 --> 42:13.239
Why are you looking for that?

42:13.322 --> 42:15.199
I want to wear it to the ceremony.

42:16.700 --> 42:18.285
My old classmates are coming,

42:18.369 --> 42:20.955
and they're always dressed to the nines.

42:21.038 --> 42:23.499
Isn't that brooch old and kind of beat-up?

42:23.582 --> 42:24.792
You said it was real gold.

42:25.376 --> 42:27.378
Gold doesn't tarnish, so it's okay.

42:28.504 --> 42:31.298
Are you going to wear that dress?

42:31.882 --> 42:33.676
Does it look weird? Should I change?

42:34.426 --> 42:35.719
No, it's fine.

42:36.637 --> 42:37.930
Where did you put it?

42:38.013 --> 42:41.225
If I knew that, I'd have found it already.
Where could it be?

42:41.308 --> 42:42.810
It's so strange.

42:43.394 --> 42:46.522
Let me look. Sometimes other people
can find these things faster.

42:47.106 --> 42:48.148
Did you look here?

42:48.232 --> 42:50.693
I wore it over my hanbok
at your cousin's wedding.

42:52.736 --> 42:53.737
So where is it?

42:54.363 --> 42:55.364
Here?

42:56.198 --> 42:57.366
I put it somewhere.

42:59.702 --> 43:00.578
Mom.

43:01.078 --> 43:04.123
Why didn't you use the cosmetics
that I sent you from the US?

43:04.206 --> 43:06.584
I was keeping them for a special occasion.

43:06.667 --> 43:08.627
I bought them ages ago!

43:08.711 --> 43:10.754
It's not good to use them
past the expiration dates!

43:10.838 --> 43:12.047
Put them back.

43:12.131 --> 43:14.550
I don't have time
to argue with you right now.

43:14.633 --> 43:16.677
I'm already late. I have to go now.

43:16.760 --> 43:17.678
I'll be off then.

43:20.222 --> 43:21.765
SERUM FOR BRIGHTER SKIN

43:27.396 --> 43:28.397
Come on.

43:34.236 --> 43:37.072
CONGRATULATIONS

43:37.156 --> 43:39.825
Hey, you're here!

43:39.908 --> 43:41.785
- Thank you for coming.
- Of course.

43:41.869 --> 43:44.038
Come inside, girls.

43:44.121 --> 43:46.165
- My goodness!
- Seung-hyo.

43:46.248 --> 43:48.834
- Thanks for coming.
- It's amazing!

43:48.917 --> 43:50.419
It's beautiful.

43:50.502 --> 43:52.880
The building looks amazing.

43:52.963 --> 43:54.298
Tell me about it.

43:54.381 --> 43:56.050
It looks incredible.

43:56.592 --> 43:57.426
Go on, get inside.

43:57.509 --> 44:00.554
I can't believe that picky little kid
grew up to be such a successful man.

44:01.513 --> 44:02.765
I'm proud of you.

44:02.848 --> 44:04.683
I'm just the CEO for show.

44:04.767 --> 44:06.477
This guy here is the real boss.

44:06.560 --> 44:08.270
Hello, ma'am.

44:08.354 --> 44:10.272
I knew you were back in Korea,
but I didn't get to meet you.

44:10.356 --> 44:12.358
She's Seung-hyo's mother, not me.

44:12.441 --> 44:13.901
I'm just her friend.

44:15.027 --> 44:16.153
I'm Seo Hye-suk.

44:17.112 --> 44:17.946
Nice to meet you.

44:18.030 --> 44:21.116
I'm so sorry, ma'am.
My name is Yoon Myeong-u.

44:21.700 --> 44:23.077
Looking at you now,

44:23.160 --> 44:24.870
I can see where Seung-hyo

44:24.953 --> 44:26.872
got all his good looks from.

44:26.955 --> 44:28.123
- Really?
- Yes!

44:28.207 --> 44:29.291
I hear that a lot.

44:29.375 --> 44:31.877
Aunt Mi-suk, where's Seok-ryu?

44:31.960 --> 44:33.212
- Well, she's…
- Hye-suk!

44:33.962 --> 44:35.547
- Hye-suk.
- Yeong-hee.

44:35.631 --> 44:36.882
- Hello.
- They're really here.

44:36.965 --> 44:38.092
- What now?
- Good to see you.

44:38.175 --> 44:39.426
- Hi!
- Hello.

44:39.510 --> 44:40.594
This is my son.

44:40.678 --> 44:42.054
- Say hello.
- Hello.

44:42.137 --> 44:43.889
- My goodness.
- They're my friends.

44:44.723 --> 44:47.059
- Thank you for coming.
- Do you remember me?

44:47.142 --> 44:48.227
It's nice to meet you.

44:48.310 --> 44:50.646
Hye-suk, Mi-suk, Jae-suk, and In-suk.

44:50.729 --> 44:52.898
It's been a while since I've seen you all.

44:52.981 --> 44:56.402
Yes, it's been a while
since the Hee and Suk Sisters met up.

44:56.485 --> 44:57.653
What tacky names!

44:59.196 --> 45:02.616
I don't know why we gave ourselves
those nicknames back then.

45:04.827 --> 45:06.412
Thank you for coming, everyone.

45:06.495 --> 45:09.123
Of course we'd come
to celebrate our friend's good news.

45:10.290 --> 45:13.502
Don't you have some good news too, Mi-suk?

45:13.585 --> 45:14.878
Isn't Seok-ryu getting married?

45:14.962 --> 45:17.172
Well, the thing is…

45:17.256 --> 45:19.842
Didn't you hear?
The engagement was called off.

45:20.426 --> 45:24.430
My, my. It was called off?

45:24.930 --> 45:26.014
I didn't know that.

45:26.765 --> 45:27.850
Well,

45:27.933 --> 45:29.810
I announced it in the reunion group chat

45:29.893 --> 45:32.312
since some already sent wedding gifts,
but you must have missed it.

45:32.396 --> 45:33.772
I'm sure they saw it.

45:34.690 --> 45:38.152
Didn't you say the ceremony would be
in some fancy resort in Hawaii?

45:38.235 --> 45:40.028
What went wrong?

45:40.112 --> 45:42.072
Nothing went wrong.

45:42.156 --> 45:45.117
We're just being extra cautious
since marriage is such a big deal.

45:45.200 --> 45:47.411
It would have been better
if you'd done that

45:47.494 --> 45:49.913
before the engagement in the first place.

45:50.706 --> 45:52.708
Stop being so old-fashioned.

45:52.791 --> 45:56.170
It's not like she's marrying a king
in the Joseon dynasty or something.

45:56.253 --> 45:57.963
The times have changed.

45:58.046 --> 45:59.840
It's not a crime to change your mind.

45:59.923 --> 46:02.634
Of course not.
It's better than getting married

46:02.718 --> 46:04.052
and divorcing afterward.

46:04.136 --> 46:05.137
- Right?
- Of course.

46:05.220 --> 46:07.389
- It's better this way.
- Your mindsets

46:07.473 --> 46:09.224
are even tackier than our nicknames.

46:09.308 --> 46:10.767
I didn't mean it like that.

46:10.851 --> 46:13.270
Let's not spoil the day
and talk about something else.

46:13.353 --> 46:15.481
All right. I'll raise my glass to that.

46:15.564 --> 46:16.648
It's good to see you guys.

46:16.732 --> 46:18.066
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

46:24.823 --> 46:27.451
I'm sorry. I should've been there.

46:27.534 --> 46:30.245
It's okay. I know how busy you are.

46:30.329 --> 46:32.789
All right. I have to go now.

46:33.290 --> 46:35.834
Okay. Don't skip your meals.

46:39.963 --> 46:42.007
FATHER

46:56.647 --> 47:00.067
Mi-suk was trying so hard
to look like she was fine.

47:01.068 --> 47:02.444
She's always been like that.

47:02.528 --> 47:04.154
So snobby, even though she's got squat.

47:04.988 --> 47:06.532
I feel sorry for her though.

47:06.615 --> 47:08.742
She was just as smart as Hye-suk

47:08.825 --> 47:10.536
but too poor to go to college.

47:10.619 --> 47:14.706
And look, she's still playing
second fiddle to her.

47:14.790 --> 47:17.793
Does she think her daughter's success
makes up for her own failure?

47:17.876 --> 47:19.336
"Her daughter's success"?

47:19.419 --> 47:23.173
It doesn't look so successful now
with the engagement breaking off.

47:23.257 --> 47:24.258
You're right.

47:24.758 --> 47:28.178
As they say, "like mother, like daughter."

47:28.262 --> 47:29.304
Exactly.

47:44.695 --> 47:46.196
I thought you weren't coming.

47:46.280 --> 47:49.825
I decided to just stop by for a bit.

47:50.367 --> 47:51.410
What's the difference?

47:52.286 --> 47:55.247
Look at all these guests.
Good for you, I guess.

47:56.123 --> 47:57.374
Thanks.

47:57.457 --> 47:59.793
I'll just stay here.
Can you call my mom over?

47:59.876 --> 48:01.878
You're still my guest.

48:02.504 --> 48:03.839
You even got me a gift.

48:04.548 --> 48:06.008
You brought it here?

48:06.091 --> 48:07.134
I can't toss it, can I?

48:07.884 --> 48:09.386
You're probably hungry, right?

48:09.469 --> 48:11.305
It's okay.
I'll just say hi to my mom and go.

48:14.182 --> 48:15.142
What's with you?

48:15.726 --> 48:16.602
Something's wrong.

48:17.352 --> 48:19.980
You keep glancing
as if you've done something wrong.

48:20.063 --> 48:21.815
- No, I didn't.
- You're still doing it.

48:21.898 --> 48:23.817
Is someone chasing you?

48:23.900 --> 48:25.360
I said I'm fine.

48:25.444 --> 48:26.445
Are you?

48:27.654 --> 48:28.655
Then wait here.

48:29.156 --> 48:30.699
I'll bring your mom and some food.

48:30.782 --> 48:31.992
I'm really okay.

48:32.075 --> 48:34.453
We used an expensive catering company,
so try some.

48:41.877 --> 48:43.003
Seok-ryu.

48:43.086 --> 48:43.962
Mom.

48:46.006 --> 48:47.591
- What are you doing here?
- To give you this.

48:47.674 --> 48:49.384
I found it after you left.

48:49.468 --> 48:50.969
Why would you bring it all the way here?

48:51.053 --> 48:54.097
I just thought you'd want this.

48:54.181 --> 48:55.766
You'd look better with--

48:55.849 --> 48:56.683
You should go now.

48:58.644 --> 49:00.437
Choisseung was going to
bring me something, so--

49:00.520 --> 49:01.438
Talk to him later!

49:02.189 --> 49:03.148
What's wrong?

49:03.231 --> 49:05.317
People will talk if they see you here.

49:06.818 --> 49:07.653
Mom.

49:09.196 --> 49:10.489
Are you ashamed of me?

49:12.699 --> 49:13.617
Mi-suk.

49:14.618 --> 49:15.786
Oh, it's Seok-ryu.

49:15.869 --> 49:17.204
Hello, Seok-ryu.

49:17.954 --> 49:21.166
They're about to head out,
so I was going to see them off.

49:21.750 --> 49:22.709
I see.

49:22.793 --> 49:24.211
Is this Seok-ryu?

49:24.294 --> 49:25.587
- My, my.
- Hey.

49:25.671 --> 49:27.422
You must be Mi-suk's daughter.

49:28.423 --> 49:30.133
It's nice to meet you.

49:30.217 --> 49:32.177
We're your mother's
high school classmates.

49:32.260 --> 49:35.222
I'm glad we ran into you.
I wanted to introduce you to her anyway.

49:35.305 --> 49:36.848
Say hello to my friends.

49:36.932 --> 49:38.642
Hello, my name is Bae Seok-ryu.

49:39.226 --> 49:40.769
- Hello.
- She's so pretty.

49:41.561 --> 49:43.522
I told you she worked for Greip, didn't I?

49:44.481 --> 49:45.941
But she recently quit.

49:46.024 --> 49:48.068
But that's such a prestigious company.

49:48.151 --> 49:49.778
Yes, she's unemployed now.

49:52.823 --> 49:55.200
Just kidding, of course!

49:56.493 --> 49:58.161
She's taking a break between jobs.

49:58.245 --> 50:01.164
She got scouted by an even better company.

50:01.665 --> 50:03.250
Really? What company?

50:03.333 --> 50:05.544
I can't keep track of them all.

50:05.627 --> 50:07.462
I'll tell you once it's decided.

50:07.546 --> 50:08.880
Is she going back to the US?

50:08.964 --> 50:11.133
Of course. That's her home.

50:12.008 --> 50:15.262
I want to spend as much time with her
as I can while she's here

50:15.345 --> 50:16.847
and make her lots of good food.

50:16.930 --> 50:19.182
I feel so bad for how skinny she is.

50:19.808 --> 50:21.601
- I know, right?
- Yes.

50:21.685 --> 50:23.395
When she told them she was quitting,

50:23.478 --> 50:26.189
they offered her more money
to make her stay.

50:26.273 --> 50:28.275
But she chose to go
to a better place anyway.

50:29.109 --> 50:30.193
Good for her.

50:53.300 --> 50:54.718
You're very good at lying.

50:55.761 --> 50:57.012
Did you practice that in advance

50:57.095 --> 50:58.263
in case I disgraced you?

50:58.346 --> 50:59.973
I didn't lie.

51:00.056 --> 51:01.266
You'll go back to the US.

51:01.850 --> 51:03.810
- What?
- I'll buy you a ticket,

51:03.894 --> 51:06.646
so pack up
and go back to the US right now.

51:07.689 --> 51:09.149
You don't want me here, do you?

51:10.317 --> 51:11.943
You never wanted me to come back.

51:12.027 --> 51:13.445
That's why you got rid of my room.

51:13.528 --> 51:15.238
That's a different issue.

51:15.322 --> 51:17.365
Why are you whining
about your room like a child?

51:17.449 --> 51:19.409
This room tells me
everything I need to know.

51:19.493 --> 51:21.244
You didn't want me to come back at all!

51:21.328 --> 51:23.163
That's right! So pack your bags.

51:23.246 --> 51:24.748
- Mom!
- Aren't you going to?

51:24.831 --> 51:27.334
Then I'll do it for you. Where's your bag?

51:28.668 --> 51:30.295
What are you doing, Mom?

51:30.378 --> 51:31.797
- Let go.
- Don't do this.

51:32.589 --> 51:33.965
I'm not going!

51:34.466 --> 51:36.051
- You are.
- No, I'm not!

51:36.134 --> 51:38.303
- I said I'm not going!
- Let go!

51:47.354 --> 51:48.563
Are you out of your mind?

51:49.940 --> 51:50.982
You're darn right I am.

51:51.608 --> 51:54.277
You're the one
who drove me out of my mind.

51:54.361 --> 51:56.988
- What did I even do?
- Do you have to ask?

51:57.072 --> 52:00.700
I really don't know why you're acting
like I committed some big crime!

52:00.784 --> 52:01.618
Hey.

52:02.369 --> 52:05.956
How could you do this to me
after everything I did to raise you right?

52:07.624 --> 52:08.625
The way I saw it,

52:09.376 --> 52:11.044
no matter how pathetic my life was,

52:11.920 --> 52:14.589
I could bear anything
as long as you were doing well.

52:15.257 --> 52:17.801
So what if my life is like this?

52:17.884 --> 52:19.553
My daughter is living a great life.

52:20.178 --> 52:22.389
But how could you betray me like this?

52:23.181 --> 52:24.766
You stabbed me in the back!

52:24.850 --> 52:28.687
Is my breaking off the engagement
and quitting my job

52:28.770 --> 52:30.146
betraying you?

52:30.230 --> 52:33.316
Yes, that's right.
I don't even want to see your face.

52:33.400 --> 52:35.944
You're sleeping all day
and fooling around like an idiot.

52:36.027 --> 52:37.863
Doesn't it ever occur to you to wonder…

52:39.197 --> 52:40.532
how sleep-deprived I must've been?

52:42.242 --> 52:44.744
Or how little fun I must have had
all these years

52:44.828 --> 52:45.996
to fool around like that?

52:46.079 --> 52:48.248
Everyone has it hard. You're not special.

52:48.331 --> 52:49.916
Even if that's the case…

52:51.710 --> 52:53.503
can't you just be on my side?

52:55.171 --> 52:56.089
Mom!

52:58.300 --> 53:00.010
I came home because I was exhausted.

53:02.596 --> 53:05.307
You know how hard I've been working.

53:05.891 --> 53:06.892
So why can't you…

53:08.393 --> 53:10.186
just tell me I did a good job,

53:10.270 --> 53:11.855
and let me take a break?

53:11.938 --> 53:15.358
Of course I know
how hard you've been working.

53:15.442 --> 53:16.526
That's why I'm so mad!

53:17.027 --> 53:18.820
While other people paid to go to the US,

53:18.904 --> 53:20.280
you got a full scholarship

53:20.363 --> 53:22.240
and earned your living expenses yourself.

53:22.324 --> 53:25.368
But now you're letting
all that hard work go to waste.

53:25.994 --> 53:27.954
I can't just let that stand.

53:28.038 --> 53:29.664
You're my precious daughter.

53:29.748 --> 53:31.458
You're my pride and joy!

53:31.541 --> 53:32.542
Why do I…

53:33.877 --> 53:36.796
Why do I always have to be
your pride and joy?

53:37.923 --> 53:40.258
Can't I just be your daughter for once,

53:40.842 --> 53:42.886
no matter how
pathetic or flawed I might be?

53:45.847 --> 53:48.850
Why do I have to cover up for your life?

54:33.812 --> 54:34.646
Jeez.

54:35.522 --> 54:37.565
You look like a ghost in a horror movie.

54:37.649 --> 54:38.483
You scared me.

54:41.444 --> 54:42.904
How did you know I was here?

54:42.988 --> 54:45.281
You're too unimaginative
to go anywhere else.

54:47.826 --> 54:50.328
The playground got so much nicer.

54:50.954 --> 54:52.539
It might as well be Disneyland.

54:54.541 --> 54:57.002
What should I play with next?

54:57.085 --> 54:58.586
Hey, wanna ride the seesaw with me?

54:58.670 --> 54:59.963
No, but knock yourself out.

55:00.046 --> 55:01.673
I can't go on the seesaw by myself.

55:02.298 --> 55:03.299
What about the jungle gym?

55:03.842 --> 55:06.678
Oh, that's right.
You used to be scared of that.

55:06.761 --> 55:07.887
That's not true.

55:07.971 --> 55:08.888
You're still scared.

55:08.972 --> 55:10.348
- No, I'm not!
- You are.

55:16.521 --> 55:18.606
What's so scary about this?

55:18.690 --> 55:20.817
- Looking for me?
- You startled me.

55:21.401 --> 55:22.569
When did you climb up?

55:23.361 --> 55:26.031
Do you think I'm still the little kid
you used to know?

55:27.032 --> 55:29.284
No, you're a tall man now.

55:30.201 --> 55:31.995
You got so tall, old man.

55:32.537 --> 55:34.956
Of course. I'm 34 already.

55:37.459 --> 55:38.460
I guess we are.

55:43.131 --> 55:46.009
This jungle gym looked so big
when I was little.

55:52.015 --> 55:54.642
Remember what you always said
whenever you were at the top?

55:55.727 --> 55:58.104
You said you wanted to
eat the clouds like cotton candy

55:58.188 --> 56:00.607
and crunch on the stars
like they were candies.

56:02.317 --> 56:03.151
I remember.

56:05.320 --> 56:08.782
I thought I'd get tall enough
to touch the sky when I got older.

56:11.910 --> 56:13.161
But there's just no way.

56:21.878 --> 56:22.712
It's raining.

56:37.185 --> 56:38.228
You're such a nuisance.

56:42.023 --> 56:45.235
Did you only buy one umbrella?

56:45.318 --> 56:49.155
Yeah, I really hate buying umbrellas
at convenience stores.

56:50.198 --> 56:52.200
You just had to get a tiny one.
Let me get under it.

56:52.283 --> 56:53.660
Go away.

56:53.743 --> 56:55.453
Just put up with it.

56:55.537 --> 56:57.163
I told you we should get down!

56:57.247 --> 56:59.082
No way. I want to keep playing!

57:09.050 --> 57:11.219
- Hey.
- Why are you laughing by yourself?

57:11.302 --> 57:12.804
I thought of something funny.

57:12.887 --> 57:13.972
Do you remember

57:14.889 --> 57:18.393
when I left you up here all alone
and ran away

57:18.476 --> 57:20.186
when we were little?

57:20.270 --> 57:23.398
You stayed here all night crying

57:23.481 --> 57:27.026
until some juvenile delinquents
who came for a smoke helped you out.

57:27.110 --> 57:28.653
They were nice guys.

57:28.736 --> 57:29.821
"Nice guys"?

57:31.364 --> 57:34.242
They were a group of thugs!

57:34.325 --> 57:36.327
- No, they weren't.
- Come on.

57:36.411 --> 57:39.247
They were obviously thugs
out to have a smoke.

57:39.330 --> 57:40.498
Then do you also remember

57:41.082 --> 57:43.835
that there used to be
a merry-go-round right there?

57:43.918 --> 57:46.045
And one time…

57:47.297 --> 57:48.798
I hit my head against it

57:49.632 --> 57:52.343
and got a huge bump
that made me look like an alien.

57:52.427 --> 57:54.596
I couldn't even look…

57:55.930 --> 57:58.099
I couldn't look in the mirror for a while.

57:58.183 --> 58:02.187
The kids said that the merry-go-round
would turn into a time machine

58:02.270 --> 58:04.439
if you spun it hard enough.

58:04.522 --> 58:06.441
I really believed that, you know.

58:06.524 --> 58:08.234
That's why I…

58:10.528 --> 58:12.071
It's so funny I'm about to cry.

58:16.534 --> 58:18.244
Hey, it's still raining.

58:19.746 --> 58:21.581
Just pick one thing.

58:21.664 --> 58:22.665
What?

58:23.833 --> 58:26.336
Don't force yourself to laugh
if you feel like crying.

01:00:19.824 --> 01:00:20.950
What an idiot.

01:00:23.911 --> 01:00:25.163
What a complete idiot.

01:01:14.587 --> 01:01:16.673
Gross, you're getting snot
all over your sleeve.

01:01:18.549 --> 01:01:20.593
It's not snot, it's rainwater.

01:01:20.677 --> 01:01:22.845
The rain washed it all away.

01:01:24.597 --> 01:01:27.517
Your makeup also got washed away.
You look horrible.

01:01:29.477 --> 01:01:32.522
Who cares?
I don't have to look nice for you.

01:01:39.404 --> 01:01:40.738
You heard our fight, right?

01:01:40.822 --> 01:01:43.157
Your voice was too loud for me to miss it.

01:01:43.241 --> 01:01:44.534
You're so annoying.

01:01:44.617 --> 01:01:45.743
Just forget everything.

01:01:46.577 --> 01:01:47.495
Already forgotten.

01:01:55.586 --> 01:01:56.879
My mom hates me.

01:01:59.966 --> 01:02:01.509
You hate her too right now.

01:02:02.927 --> 01:02:04.220
Isn't it pathetic

01:02:05.304 --> 01:02:07.140
that I still hate my mom at my age?

01:02:15.398 --> 01:02:16.232
Did you know?

01:02:18.025 --> 01:02:20.027
Just like how the moon
is Earth's satellite,

01:02:20.820 --> 01:02:22.530
hate has its own satellites.

01:02:25.158 --> 01:02:27.326
Your high expectations, your faith,

01:02:27.869 --> 01:02:30.371
and your fondness for a certain person

01:02:30.997 --> 01:02:32.081
are all interconnected.

01:02:33.499 --> 01:02:36.085
But when any of those elements
leave orbit or retrograde,

01:02:36.169 --> 01:02:37.420
it can turn into hate.

01:02:40.131 --> 01:02:42.467
You can't hate someone
unless you love them.

01:02:49.432 --> 01:02:50.308
What is it?

01:02:51.392 --> 01:02:52.769
- Did you see that?
- See what?

01:02:52.852 --> 01:02:54.187
A shooting star.

01:02:54.937 --> 01:02:56.814
There was a shooting star just now!

01:02:57.482 --> 01:02:58.775
You were just seeing things.

01:02:58.858 --> 01:03:00.777
I know what I saw!

01:03:00.860 --> 01:03:04.071
Look! There was another one!

01:03:04.155 --> 01:03:05.698
- I saw it.
- Right?

01:03:06.199 --> 01:03:07.700
- That's so cool.
- Make a wish.

01:03:08.910 --> 01:03:10.495
That's so childish.

01:03:29.472 --> 01:03:30.473
What did you wish for?

01:03:30.556 --> 01:03:32.517
I wished that my company
wouldn't go under.

01:03:33.601 --> 01:03:35.645
I know you're just showing off.

01:03:35.728 --> 01:03:37.396
Why would your company go…

01:03:40.191 --> 01:03:41.526
Something happened, right?

01:03:43.653 --> 01:03:46.697
- I'm right, aren't I?
- You're so violent.

01:03:48.825 --> 01:03:49.909
It's just that

01:03:51.494 --> 01:03:53.204
I took a big risk…

01:03:55.081 --> 01:03:57.458
and I'm afraid I'll end up
falling on my face.

01:03:59.293 --> 01:04:00.670
We have no new clients,

01:04:01.671 --> 01:04:03.464
and we're not getting
the design fees either.

01:04:04.090 --> 01:04:04.924
Let's go.

01:04:05.007 --> 01:04:06.843
Right now? Where?

01:04:07.552 --> 01:04:10.888
Just tell me who owes you money.
I'll make them cough it up.

01:04:12.098 --> 01:04:13.057
How will you do that?

01:04:13.140 --> 01:04:14.308
I won't leave until they do.

01:04:15.268 --> 01:04:18.020
I should've gotten
a scary tattoo or something.

01:04:18.521 --> 01:04:21.482
I know. I should change
into animal-print clothes before we go.

01:04:22.024 --> 01:04:24.527
I'm sure my mom has some in her closet.

01:04:24.610 --> 01:04:26.404
You're really something else.

01:04:26.988 --> 01:04:28.030
So where should I go?

01:04:28.114 --> 01:04:29.574
Let's go to a food stall.

01:04:30.116 --> 01:04:31.117
Let's have some udon.

01:04:31.951 --> 01:04:32.952
Hey.

01:04:33.995 --> 01:04:35.329
Did you read my mind?

01:04:36.038 --> 01:04:37.748
How did you know

01:04:37.832 --> 01:04:41.043
that I wished for the nearby food stall
to still be open?

01:04:41.127 --> 01:04:43.004
Who wishes for something like that?

01:04:43.087 --> 01:04:44.338
I do.

01:04:44.422 --> 01:04:47.174
Let's go get your money
after we eat some udon.

01:04:47.258 --> 01:04:49.594
I guess I can't ever go under now.

01:04:49.677 --> 01:04:52.680
I'll have to push through everything
no matter what.

01:04:53.180 --> 01:04:54.181
Why's that?

01:04:54.849 --> 01:04:58.436
Because I don't ever want to see you
wearing leopard-print clothes.

01:04:58.519 --> 01:05:00.646
Are you worried
that I'd look too hot for you?

01:05:00.730 --> 01:05:03.858
You know what would happen
if you wore something like that?

01:05:03.941 --> 01:05:05.443
You'd get shot down and hunted.

01:05:06.360 --> 01:05:08.446
Do you want to die,
bite the dust, or perish?

01:05:08.529 --> 01:05:09.530
I'd rather eat udon.

01:05:15.494 --> 01:05:16.329
Seok-ryu.

01:05:19.373 --> 01:05:20.833
Where did she go so early?

01:05:30.384 --> 01:05:34.263
YOON MYEONG-U

01:05:34.347 --> 01:05:35.514
- Mr. Yoon.
- Yes?

01:05:35.598 --> 01:05:38.267
I talked to the client from Buryeong-dong,

01:05:38.351 --> 01:05:40.811
and he decided to
keep the windows facing east.

01:05:40.895 --> 01:05:43.064
Really? How did you convince him?

01:05:43.147 --> 01:05:45.232
I just told him
that having east-facing windows

01:05:45.316 --> 01:05:47.360
would bring in good fortune and money.

01:05:47.443 --> 01:05:48.861
What?

01:05:49.654 --> 01:05:51.280
Did that really work?

01:05:51.364 --> 01:05:52.365
Yes.

01:05:54.116 --> 01:05:56.369
But where's Seung-hyo?

01:05:56.452 --> 01:05:58.120
I miss him so much.

01:05:58.204 --> 01:06:00.331
I don't know.
He hasn't been in the whole day.

01:06:00.414 --> 01:06:02.708
Yes, you can put that here.

01:06:02.792 --> 01:06:04.835
YOON MYEONG-U

01:06:08.965 --> 01:06:10.549
You're home, Seok-ryu.

01:06:10.633 --> 01:06:13.052
Hurry up and get changed
so we can have dinner.

01:06:13.135 --> 01:06:14.303
I'm not hungry.

01:06:26.065 --> 01:06:27.274
Mom.

01:06:29.360 --> 01:06:30.611
Mom!

01:06:37.493 --> 01:06:39.412
Mom!

01:06:40.871 --> 01:06:41.872
Mom!

01:06:41.956 --> 01:06:45.001
Why don't you yell for your dad for once?

01:06:45.084 --> 01:06:46.293
Sure, Dad. Mom!

01:06:46.377 --> 01:06:48.129
What happened to my room?

01:06:48.212 --> 01:06:50.506
Pipe down already.

01:06:50.589 --> 01:06:51.924
Go and wash your hands.

01:06:52.717 --> 01:06:54.719
Your mom asked Seung-hyo to do that.

01:07:00.933 --> 01:07:02.727
What is it, Aunt Mi-suk?

01:07:02.810 --> 01:07:05.604
I have a commission for you, Seung-hyo.

01:07:05.688 --> 01:07:09.150
- Can you redecorate Seok-ryu's room?
- What?

01:07:09.233 --> 01:07:13.112
I can't have her sleep in the storage
like she's a piece of luggage.

01:07:13.612 --> 01:07:16.991
Whether it's for a few days
or a few months, she deserves a room.

01:07:17.908 --> 01:07:19.201
I approve wholeheartedly.

01:07:33.674 --> 01:07:35.259
The walls should be green

01:07:35.342 --> 01:07:38.304
but with some tree patterns like this.

01:07:38.804 --> 01:07:40.264
Do you have something similar?

01:07:40.347 --> 01:07:41.390
Of course.

01:07:42.933 --> 01:07:44.810
It's an old-fashioned design,

01:07:44.894 --> 01:07:47.063
but please keep to it
as closely as possible.

01:07:47.146 --> 01:07:51.108
I think we have what you need right here.

01:07:51.192 --> 01:07:52.193
Thanks.

01:07:52.943 --> 01:07:54.028
YOON MYEONG-U

01:07:57.114 --> 01:07:58.908
Where should we put this?

01:07:58.991 --> 01:08:01.577
Put it close to the wall, please.

01:08:01.660 --> 01:08:02.661
- Here?
- Yes.

01:08:03.245 --> 01:08:06.749
You should've told me
that you were going to redo my room.

01:08:06.832 --> 01:08:08.751
I was going to tell you in the morning,
but you weren't home.

01:08:09.877 --> 01:08:11.712
Where were you all day?

01:08:11.796 --> 01:08:12.838
Just here and there.

01:08:12.922 --> 01:08:15.091
She must have had some business.
Let's eat.

01:08:15.966 --> 01:08:17.134
Look at that.

01:08:19.553 --> 01:08:20.554
Here.

01:08:25.976 --> 01:08:26.811
Eat.

01:08:28.312 --> 01:08:30.064
- Honey.
- Thanks.

01:08:30.147 --> 01:08:31.565
Thank you for the food.

01:08:31.649 --> 01:08:34.068
Why did you make abalone rice?
Wasn't it expensive?

01:08:34.151 --> 01:08:35.319
Don't you worry.

01:08:35.402 --> 01:08:37.113
Nothing is too expensive for my daughter!

01:08:37.196 --> 01:08:38.030
Eat up.

01:08:43.410 --> 01:08:44.787
It's so good.

01:08:44.870 --> 01:08:46.080
It's unbelievably good!

01:08:46.163 --> 01:08:47.414
It is, right?

01:08:47.498 --> 01:08:48.666
Have some braised short ribs.

01:08:50.709 --> 01:08:53.379
- This is incredible.
- You like this too, don't you?

01:08:53.462 --> 01:08:55.214
- It's eggplant.
- Have some.

01:08:55.297 --> 01:08:57.049
- It's your favorite.
- I'll give you some more.

01:08:57.133 --> 01:08:58.926
Slow down before she chokes.

01:08:59.009 --> 01:09:00.845
Stop hitting me!

01:09:00.928 --> 01:09:03.472
What's with this unnaturally
happy family vibe?

01:09:03.556 --> 01:09:05.307
You're just in time. Wash your hands.

01:09:05.808 --> 01:09:08.185
I told you I'm on a diet, Mom.

01:09:09.645 --> 01:09:11.147
Shut up and eat.

01:09:11.897 --> 01:09:15.484
If you two fight again,
I'll kick you out immediately.

01:09:16.110 --> 01:09:17.194
- Sit.
- All right.

01:09:17.278 --> 01:09:18.237
- Sit.
- Okay.

01:09:19.405 --> 01:09:21.073
Here, try some of this too.

01:09:21.157 --> 01:09:23.742
Didn't you hear your mom
tell you to wash your hands?

01:09:23.826 --> 01:09:26.453
You should wash them in the bathroom.

01:09:26.537 --> 01:09:27.913
Give this to Seok-ryu.

01:09:27.997 --> 01:09:29.874
There you go. Eat up.

01:09:30.791 --> 01:09:32.126
It's really good.

01:09:32.209 --> 01:09:33.252
It really is.

01:11:11.183 --> 01:11:12.935
Hey, it's the middle of the night.

01:11:13.018 --> 01:11:15.562
What's with the stars on the ceiling?

01:11:15.646 --> 01:11:18.482
Shouldn't you be thanking me first?

01:11:18.565 --> 01:11:20.442
You're so meticulous.

01:11:21.026 --> 01:11:23.445
How did you even recreate
the stars on the ceiling?

01:11:23.529 --> 01:11:25.698
Just the stars?
What about everything else?

01:11:25.781 --> 01:11:27.449
Everything else too.

01:11:28.033 --> 01:11:29.910
Did you work some magic on my room?

01:11:29.994 --> 01:11:31.453
I turned back time.

01:11:31.537 --> 01:11:34.456
The desk where you wrote
a love letter to your senior.

01:11:34.540 --> 01:11:36.709
The bed you cried on
after he rejected you.

01:11:36.792 --> 01:11:38.335
The blanket you used to kick
in embarrassment.

01:11:38.419 --> 01:11:40.129
I recreated your embarrassing past.

01:11:40.212 --> 01:11:42.256
Damn it, I remember everything now.

01:11:42.339 --> 01:11:45.926
No, stop! Go back
to the realm of the subconscious!

01:11:46.010 --> 01:11:49.680
I need to stop remembering
all those embarrassing things!

01:11:49.763 --> 01:11:51.473
I have a favor to ask.

01:11:51.557 --> 01:11:53.684
Make sure your curtains
are drawn shut properly from now on.

01:11:53.767 --> 01:11:54.935
What?

01:11:56.145 --> 01:11:58.230
I'm all over the place. It's so hot.

01:12:04.987 --> 01:12:05.988
Wait, what?

01:12:06.655 --> 01:12:07.614
Why are you there?

01:12:07.698 --> 01:12:08.824
This is why.

01:12:08.907 --> 01:12:12.786
I don't want to see anything unpleasant
whenever I open the window.

01:12:12.870 --> 01:12:14.580
Your bed hair and your bare face,

01:12:15.372 --> 01:12:16.248
for example.

01:12:17.082 --> 01:12:21.045
I was actually feeling grateful
toward you for a second there.

01:12:21.128 --> 01:12:22.755
But forget it. I'm coming over.

01:12:26.091 --> 01:12:27.092
By the way,

01:12:27.676 --> 01:12:29.636
why are you worried
about your view anyway?

01:12:30.137 --> 01:12:31.221
You don't even live there.

01:12:31.930 --> 01:12:32.848
I moved back here.

01:12:33.474 --> 01:12:34.308
What?

01:12:35.059 --> 01:12:36.101
I live here now.

01:13:26.068 --> 01:13:31.949
HATE

01:13:32.032 --> 01:13:36.703
LOVE

01:14:08.986 --> 01:14:13.365
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:14:13.449 --> 01:14:17.035
You know that people who have jobs
actually work during the day, right?

01:14:17.619 --> 01:14:18.871
What should we do now?

01:14:18.954 --> 01:14:20.998
Are you both leaving me here?

01:14:21.582 --> 01:14:22.499
I want to do this.

01:14:22.583 --> 01:14:24.585
You joined the design contest
to rebuild the gym

01:14:24.668 --> 01:14:26.503
and construct a new school building?

01:14:27.087 --> 01:14:28.505
What was your original dream?

01:14:28.589 --> 01:14:30.132
My dream?

01:14:30.215 --> 01:14:32.134
We're transferring an emergency patient.

01:14:32.217 --> 01:14:34.553
I think he's trying to clear the way.

01:14:34.636 --> 01:14:37.473
If you could swim again,

01:14:37.556 --> 01:14:39.099
would you still be an architect?

01:14:39.183 --> 01:14:41.894
What's the big deal
about that old time capsule?

01:14:41.977 --> 01:14:43.604
Aren't you curious to know what it says?

01:14:43.687 --> 01:14:44.813
I told you not to do it!

01:14:46.315 --> 01:14:47.900
Come and get it then.

01:14:50.861 --> 01:14:55.866
Subtitle translation by: Ji-yeun Kim
